// Package vendor holds the do-not-edit banner stamped onto a consumer
// domain's generated spec/registrydump/main.go (task #367,
// `hotam scaffold-registrydump` -- cmd/hotam/scaffold_registrydump.go).
//
// Unlike internal/recorder/vendor and internal/ontology/vendor, this
// package's banner does not sit in front of a byte-for-byte VENDORED copy of
// a canon source file -- spec/registrydump/main.go is a small, per-domain
// TEMPLATED program (its import path is substituted with the domain's own
// spec/ module path), so there is no single canonicalSource to embed here.
// The banner constant is still factored into its own leaf package, same as
// the other two, for exactly one reason: internal/gate/model_scan.go's
// unified generated-file exclusion (BuildAuthoredModels' scanDomainModelFiles)
// needs to recognize this banner's first line alongside
// internal/recorder/vendor.Banner and internal/ontology/vendor.Banner
// WITHOUT internal/gate importing cmd/hotam -- an import cmd/hotam already
// makes in the other direction (cmd/hotam -> internal/gate, e.g.
// cmd/hotam/main.go, cmd/hotam/sync_domain.go), so internal/gate importing
// cmd/hotam back would close a cycle. Lifting just the banner into this
// shared leaf package (both cmd/hotam and internal/gate import it directly;
// neither imports the other) routes around that cycle exactly the way
// internal/recorder/vendor and internal/ontology/vendor already do for their
// own banners.
package vendor

// Banner is the do-not-edit banner prepended to every generated
// spec/registrydump/main.go -- same rhetorical shape as
// internal/recorder/vendor.Banner / internal/ontology/vendor.Banner, applied
// here to a GENERATED (not vendored-from-canon) file: hand-editing it will
// be silently discarded the next time `hotam scaffold-registrydump` runs.
//
// cmd/hotam/scaffold_registrydump.go is the single writer of files carrying
// this banner (registrydumpSource prepends it to the templated program
// body); internal/gate/model_scan.go is the only OTHER package that
// references this constant, and only to recognize -- never to write -- a
// file stamped with it.
const Banner = `// Code generated by ` + "`hotam scaffold-registrydump`" + `. DO NOT EDIT.
//
// This program is the domain-side half of the module-boundary bridge
// ` + "`hotam sync-domain`" + ` uses to read this domain's own Go-authored Requirement
// registry (declared in this spec/ module's root package, conventionally
// spec/requirements.go, as ` + "`var Requirements = hotamontology.New[hotamontology.Requirement]()`" + `,
// mirroring internal/selfspec.Requirements' shape in the HotamSpec engine
// itself) without the engine ever needing a cross-module Go import into this
// domain's separate spec/ module (forbidden -- see
// internal/gate/test_exec.go's module-boundary doc comments for the
// identical constraint applied to verified_by test execution).
//
// ` + "`hotam sync-domain`" + ` spawns this program via ` + "`go run ./registrydump`" + ` inside this
// module and reads its stdout as JSON.
`
